  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Government of Papua New Guinea pro bono legal training</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In July 2024, AGS lawyers delivered 5 days of pro bono training on legal research, writing, statutory interpretation, and presentation skills to lawyers from the PNG Office of the State Solicitor in Port Moresby. In October 2024, AGS lawyers delivered 5 days of training on procurement, contract basics, and complex contract issues. In March&#x2013;April 2025, AGS lawyers delivered 8 days of training on ICT contracts, leases, infrastructure-related contracting, risk management, governance, and legislative drafting. In April 2025, an AGS lawyer delivered a Continuing Legal Education seminar, sponsored by the PNG Law Society, to over 80 PNG lawyers, including those from the State Solicitor&#x2019;s Office, international firms, and private practice. In May 2025, an AGS lawyer attended the PNG Office of the Solicitor General for 2 weeks to conduct a practice management review.</narrative>
  </description>
